  <h3>Evaluation Model</h3>
  <p>Providers are lazily created, dependencies are wired by <code>ref.watch()</code>, and listeners are updated only when the exposed value changes. This makes Riverpod closer to a scoped provider graph than to a single store with selectors.</p>

  <h3>Trade-offs</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strengths:</strong> Auto-tracking via ref.watch(), rich provider type system, code generation support, ProviderScope for testing</li>
    <li><strong>Weaknesses:</strong> Flutter-only, provider lifecycle and scope rules take time to learn, ProviderScope boilerplate</li>
  </ul>

