  <!-- swift-state-graph -->
  <h2 id="swift-state-graph">swift-state-graph</h2>
  <p class="not-prose text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://github.com/VergeGroup/swift-state-graph" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">github.com/VergeGroup/swift-state-graph</a></p>

  <p><strong>Platform:</strong> Swift 6.0+ (SwiftUI &amp; UIKit) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Pattern:</strong> DAG-based graph</p>

  <p>swift-state-graph models state as a <strong>directed acyclic graph (DAG)</strong>. Its current public API uses <code>@GraphStored</code> properties for source state and <code>@GraphComputed</code> properties for derived state on a <code>GraphObject</code>, with ThreadLocal-based tracking for dependency discovery and lazy invalidation for reads.</p>

